.TH BLANKRES 1 "September 2026" "blankres 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blankres \- review and send crash reports
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blankres
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ REPORT ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reviews crash reports that
.BR blankresd (8)
has left awaiting a decision, and sends them if you choose to. It is the terminal equivalent of
.BR blankres-gtk (1)
and applies the same rules: a report is only ever uploaded by an explicit
.B send
command.
.PP
.I REPORT
may be a path or, when unambiguous, just the program name.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List crashes waiting for a decision.
.TP
.BI show " REPORT"
Print every field that would be transmitted, including the size of the memory snapshot.
.TP
.BI send " REPORT"
Upload the report, then delete it and its core dump.
.TP
.BI discard " REPORT"
Delete the report and its core dump without sending anything.
.TP
.BI ignore " REPORT"
Discard it and record the signature so this problem is never raised again.
.TP
.B ignored
List the signatures this user has chosen to ignore.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Configuration file. Default
.IR /etc/blankres/client.json .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Non-zero if the named report does not exist, is ambiguous, or could not be uploaded.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR blankresd (8),
.BR blankres-gtk (1)
